<title>SPAIN: Spain's Sol Melia Q1 attributable up 41 pct.</title>
<headline>Spain's Sol Melia Q1 attributable up 41 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for the first quarter, in billions of pesetas, unless stated:</p>
<p> Attributable profit			 1.21    vs    0.86</p>
<p> Total revenues				2.84    vs    2.47</p>
<p> Ordinary profit			     1.60    vs    1.26</p>
<p>    Total expenditures		     1.391    vs   1.133</p>
<p>    EBTDA					1.825    vs    1.407</p>
<p>    Depreciations, amortisation	  0.165    vs    0.075</p>
<p>    Profit/loss from ordinary act.     1.597    vs    1.260</p>
<p>    Profit before tax and minorities   1.601    vs    1.260</p>
<p>    Parent company profit		  1.213    vs    0.860</p>
<p>NOTE - As March 1997, Sol Melia manages 212 hoteles, having signed a further 14 contracts to be under operations before year end. In turn, there are 20 further contracts signed for hotel additions to take place in 1998 and 1999.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
